2026-06-11 21:12:35 | DEBUG    | openai._base_client | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Helper-Method': 'chat.completions.parse', 'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a21c4819-d008-4c2b-8daf-5a19a99a5e85', 'post_parser': <function Completions.parse.<locals>.parser at 0x000001FC8D8194E0>, 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': "You are a strict relevance judge for an information retrieval benchmark.\n\nYour task is to determine whether a candidate book satisfies the user's search intent.\n\nFocus on intent matching, not merely thematic similarity.\n\nScoring rubric:\n\n2 - HIGHLY RELEVANT\n\n* The book directly satisfies the query.\n* The main topic, genre, subject, setting, character type, or information need closely matches the query.\n* A user issuing this query would be very likely to click or select this book.\n\n1 - SOMEWHAT RELEVANT\n\n* The book has meaningful overlap with the query.\n* It shares some themes, genre, topics, or concepts.\n* However, it does not fully satisfy the query intent.\n* A user might consider the book as an alternative, but it is not an obvious match.\n\n0 - NOT RELEVANT\n\n* The book does not satisfy the query intent.\n* Similarity is weak, generic, incidental, or based only on broad genre overlap.\n* A user searching with this query would be unlikely to find the book useful.\n\nImportant guidelines:\n\n* Judge based on the query intent, not overall book quality.\n* Do not give score 1 simply because two books share a broad genre.\n* Prefer score 0 when overlap is weak or indirect.\n* Use score 2 sparingly and only for strong matches.\n* Be conservative when assigning relevance.\n\nAlways provide a concise reason (1-2 sentences).\n", 'role': 'system'}, {'content': 'Search Query:\nbooks discussing isolation in modern life\n\nCandidate Book:\n\nTitle: Breaking the Chains\n\nDescription:\nbreaking the chains" by Leonard L. Taylor is a thought-provoking and illuminating book on the subject of addiction. Taylor, a former addict and now a neuroscientist, challenges the traditional view that addiction is a disease of the brain, and instead argues that it is a normal response to difficult life circumstances.Taylor begins by discussing the neural pathways that are activated during addiction, explaining how the brain\'s reward system becomes hijacked by the pleasurable effects of drugs or behaviors. However, he also delves into the role of personal experiences and emotional states in the development of addiction. He cites research showing that trauma, stress, and social isolation can all increase the risk of addiction, and argues that these external factors must be considered in any effective treatment plan. One of the most compelling aspects of the book is Taylor\'s portrayal of addicts as people who are struggling with difficult emotions and trying to cope with their circumstances in the best way they know how. He presents a nuanced and compassionate view of addiction, acknowledging that addicts are not simply weak-willed or morally deficient, but rather are driven by a deep need for relief and connection. Taylor also debunks many of the myths surrounding addiction, including the idea that addicts lack self-control or that they are "addicted" to the substance itself. Instead, he argues that addiction is a complex interplay between biology, psychology, and social context, and that the best way to overcome it is through a holistic approach that addresses all of these factors. Overall, "breaking the chains" is a must-read for anyone interested in understanding addiction in a more nuanced and empathetic way. Taylor\'s scientific expertise and personal experience make for a compelling and convincing argument that will surely change the way readers think about this often misunderstood and stigmatized condition.\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
