:\nExplore the fascinating frontier of artificial intelligence and the rise of sentient machines. In Awakening Intelligence: Criteria for Sentient AI, Siamak Goudarzi, a leading voice in AI ethics and technology law, unpacks one of the most compelling questions of our time: Can machines become sentient, and what would that mean for humanity? Artificial intelligence has progressed from basic tools to sophisticated systems capable of autonomy and decision-making. But as AI grows more advanced, how do we define and recognize sentience in machines? And how should society adapt to these developments? This book dives into the scientific, philosophical, and ethical dimensions of AI sentience, offering readers a roadmap to understand and engage with this transformative field. What You'll Learn The Evolution of Artificial Sentience Understand how AI has evolved and why sentience is the next frontier. Defining Sentience Explore consciousness and awareness from philosophical and scientific perspectives, comparing biological and artificial entities. Criteria for AI Sentience Discover key benchmarks like self-awareness, emotional capacity, and intentionality-and how these apply to machines. Ethics of Sentient AI Delve into the moral and legal dilemmas: Should sentient AI have rights? What responsibilities do we owe them? Real-World AI Examples Learn from case studies like Sophia the Robot, OpenAI's GPT, and DeepMind's AlphaGo, and assess their progress toward sentience. Opportunities and Risks Explore the benefits of AI in areas like healthcare and education, alongside challenges like bias, misuse, and ethical conflicts. Why This Book Matters AI is reshaping society, yet few resources provide a balanced exploration of its potential and risks. Whether you're an AI enthusiast, professional, policymaker, or simply curious, Awakening Intelligence equips you with the tools to engage thoughtfully with AI's rapid evolution. Accessible and Thought-Provoking: Complex concepts are presented \n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user's search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
