rty\'s Adventures with the Ghost\n\nDescription:\nThe Haunted House - Kids Mystery books Ages 9-12:Bedtime stories children books for early beginner readers collection. Kids realistic fiction."You\'re the new kids who live in the Old McGregor house, aren\'t you?" the tall blonde boy asked looking at the two Allen brothers."That\'s right. I\'m Kurt and this is my little brother, Martin. Everyone calls him Marty.""I\'m Billy Kendall," responded the blond boy. "Did you know your house is haunted?""Haunted?" stammered Marty. "What does he mean, Kurt?" asked Marty."I\'ve heard the stories," responded Kurt. "But I don\'t believe in ghosts.""Well, you\'re in for a surprise, then," predicted Billy. "My brother and his buddies were up at your house one night and they heard groaning and chains clanking. Books flew off the shelves and doors slammed. They couldn\'t get out of there fast enough!">>>Ghosts that are more often friendly than frighteningThis children\'s ghost story is the perfect way to introduce young readers to the fun of being scared silly. Kids can enter the mysterious world of ghosts and Identify through the eyes of young characters, and meet ghosts that are more often friendly than frightening.>>> Just follow the heart.Everyone knows that ghosts can be scary. But have you read this kids adventure novels about brave 10 years old boy that is in adventure with the ghost? It is very interesting ghost story for kids with mystery and friendship. It is about brave 10 years old boy and through his adventure kids can learn that they should not be afraid of anything, just need to follow their heart.About the StoryDevastated by the death of her husband, mystery writer, Jennifer Allen, decides to move her sons, ten-year-old Kurt and six-year-old Marty, from their apartment in New York City to a rambling, two-hundred-year-old Victorian house in New Hope. Ignoring local legends about a ghost, Jennifer sets out to complete her latest novel. Caught up by the excitement of living in a haunted house, Marty sets out to connect to the inf\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
