mall-Town Second-Chance Romance of Friendship, Healing, and ForeverSome loves don't end. They wait-quietly-for the moment you're ready to come back. Lucas Bennett was Willow Creek's golden boy. He left town carrying ambition, expectations, and a future everyone believed in. What he didn't expect was how much he'd lose along the way-or how unfinished the past would feel when he finally returned. Maya Collins was his best friend. His first love. He's almost everything. She stayed behind, rooted in the town that had raised her, building a life shaped by loyalty, routine, and the memory of a boy who had left without explaining why. Time taught her how to survive the loss-but not how to forget it. Now Lucas is back, older and changed, and forced into proximity with the one person who still sees straight through him. Old routines resurface. Childhood memories linger. And the line between friendship and love becomes impossible to ignore. As Willow Creek faces its own changes-pressures that threaten its traditions, land, and future-Lucas and Maya must confront the truth they've both avoided: the greatest risk isn't loving each other again, but losing what they never truly stopped wanting. Set against quiet creeks, familiar streets, and a small town that remembers everything, Back to What We Were is a deeply emotional friends-to-lovers, second-chance contemporary romance about healing old wounds, choosing forgiveness, and discovering that sometimes love doesn't need a new beginning-just the courage to return. Tender, atmospheric, and rich with emotional depth, this final book delivers slow-burn intimacy, heartfelt connection, and a deeply satisfying happily-ever-after for readers who believe the strongest love stories are the ones that survive time. Perfect for readers who love: Second-chance romance novels Friends-to-lovers contemporary romance Childhood sweethearts romance Small town romance series Emotional healing love stories Forced proximity romance Found family and\n\