scription:\nEscape to Oakhaven, where the pines are tall, the secrets are deep, and love is the only thing worth staying for. This massive 10-book collection brings together a series of interconnected, heart-wrenching, and steamy romances set in the ruggedly beautiful town of Oakhaven. From rivals-to-lovers and grumpy-meets-sunshine to childhood trauma and slow-burn second chances, these stories explore the healing power of being seen for who you truly are. Whether it\'s a lighthouse keeper guarding more than just the coast or a bookstore owner who knows exactly what you need before you do, these men are ready to fight for their "happily ever afters." Dive into emotional, character-driven romance where every scar has a story and every home is built to last. The Collection Includes: The Bookstore Owner Who Memorized My Order Caleb, the owner of The Dusty Page, knows everything about his favorite customer, Julian Thorne. When Julian\'s past as a high-stakes architect catches up with him, they must decide if their connection is a liability or the foundation of a new life together. The Boy Who Came Back Different Silas Thorne returns to Oakhaven after a decade away to settle his father\'s estate and leave. Instead, he finds himself trapped in the town\'s literal and metaphorical shadows, finding safety only in the arms of Elias, the man who refuses to let him disappear again. The Cabin That Came With a Boyfriend After his career in San Francisco implodes, Julian seeks silence in a remote Oregon cabin. He doesn\'t expect a protective, hammer-wielding neighbor named Silas who challenges him to stop running and finally start building. The Lighthouse Keeper\'s Secret Julian, a disgraced academic, takes a job assisting the reclusive Elias Thorne at the Oakhaven Point Lighthouse. As they catalog shipwreck artifacts, they discover a supernatural secret that ties their fates-and the lighthouse itself-together. The Luminous Valley Caleb Vance needs a neighboring farm to save his family\'s orchard,\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
